> For me K=10, but the majority of probes (~85%) will match just once,
> then decaying and down to ~10s of thousands that match 10 times.

So, (chromosome, unit) takes 1+4 bytes.  With K=10 mappings, the cost
is 5*K=50 bytes per cell.  With ~6,000,000 cells, the fully expanded
file will be ~300 MB large.  Compressed it will be much smaller, but
it is of course quite large but doable.

